h264player - H.264 (baseline) video player plugin
=================================================

A fork of mpegplayer that decodes H.264 baseline profile with libh264bsd
(libh264bsd/, Apache-2.0) instead of libmpeg2. Container, audio (MP2/MP3 via
libmad), buffering, sync and UI are mpegplayer's.

Files: *.h264 (MPEG program stream, MP2/MP3 audio) or *.ts (MPEG transport
stream, AAC-LC / MP2 / MP3 audio). AAC is decoded with Rockbox's libfaad.

Encoding a compatible file
--------------------------
  ffmpeg -i in.mp4 -vf scale=320:-2 -r 24 \
    -c:v libx264 -profile:v baseline -level 2.1 -x264-params ref=3:bframes=0:keyint=48 \
    -c:a mp2 -b:a 128k -ar 44100 -f vob out.h264

Requirements: baseline profile (no B-frames, no CABAC/interlace), progressive,
a video PES id in 0xE0-0xEF (ffmpeg uses 0xE2, accepted), and keep reference
frames <= 4 (each QVGA frame is ~115 KB of the 2 MiB decoder pool).
Keyframes (IDR) every ~2 s: seeking and frame-skip recovery use IDR pictures.

Testing (no device needed)
--------------------------
  test/run_all.sh    host decoder tests (native, ASan/UBSan, 32-bit,
                     mipsel/qemu, fuzz) + headless simulator runs for
                     erosqnative and rg35xxpro, all compared with ffmpeg.
Needs: ffmpeg (libx264, mp2), python3, gcc (+multilib), SDL2 dev headers,
mipsel-linux-gnu-gcc and qemu-user (optional).
The simulator runs use a sim-only hook in apps/main.c (env
ROCKBOX_AUTORUN_PLUGIN / ROCKBOX_AUTORUN_PARAM) and h264test.c.

Layout
------
  h264dec.[ch]   libmpeg2-shaped front end over libh264bsd (NAL reassembly,
                 PTS tagging, skip/flush semantics)
  ts_parser.[ch] MPEG-TS demuxer (PAT/PMT, per-PID payloads, PTS, seek scans)
  aac_dec.[ch]   ADTS parsing + libfaad wrapper; faad_glue.c supplies what
                 libfaad/mdct expect from the codec API (built via
                 h264player.make from lib/rbcodec/codecs/{libfaad,lib})
  video_thread.c video_out_rockbox.c mpeg_parser.c ...  from mpegplayer
